Description: Give the shared-kernel native manager a fixed private generator tmpfs context
 Preserve the original clone, slave propagation, nosuid/nodev flags, tmpfs limits,
 generator execution and child wait/error semantics. Only the actual native raw
 SELinux context selects the fixed labels. Other managers keep stock options.
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-25

